feat: rebuild the dashboard to match the new design

Ports the dashboard layout properly rather than just recolouring the old one.

- greeting + inline quick-action pills in the header, instead of a row of
  oversized action cards
- five compact stat cards (adds orphan count) on an auto-fit grid
- two-column body: recently edited / 14-day writing heat / PARA progress on
  the left, knowledge graph / tag chips / recently created on the right
- the 14-day writing heat chart and PARA progress bars are new; both were in
  the design and missing here
- mono for every label, count and timestamp; sans for content
- collapses to one column under 1040px

Also swapped the import control from a ref + .click() to a <label> wrapping
the hidden input: fewer moving parts, keyboard accessible, and it stops the
React compiler flagging a ref read during render.
